# Every text file keeps LF in the working tree, on every system.
#
# A Windows checkout (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true) would otherwise write
# CRLF. That breaks shell scripts, and the plugin's hooks are shell scripts: the shebang's
# interpreter path ends up as `/bin/sh\r`, which Git Bash cannot run, and a value read out of
# a file (the shim reads the launcher's baked bun path) keeps a trailing \r and stops
# matching. Git Bash and sh need the LF form of plugin/bin/*, and of everything else they read.
* text=auto eol=lf
